<title>USA: Philippines' National Power files $200 mln bonds.</title>
<headline>Philippines' National Power files $200 mln bonds.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Power Corp, a utility owned by the government of the Philippines, said it filed on Friday with the Securities and Exchange Commission for up to $200 million in bonds.</p>
<p>Net proceeds will be used to finance part of the company's capital expansion projects and for the rehabilitation and improvement of existing plants and other facilities, it said.</p>
<p>The offering will be made through Salomon Bros. Inc, Merrill Lynch &amp; Co and Morgan Stanley &amp; Co Inc.</p>
</text>
